### `vocabulary.yaml`

Code makes one kernel task per queue row. It checks a row's `mode`, `depends_on`, `tier`, `unit`, `site`, `surface` and how many `cells`; the workers read the rest. Keep the keys exactly.

```yaml
verdict: assemblable | assemblable_after_additions | ceiling
steps:
  - step: <what this step computes>
    values: {<axis>: <this checkpoint's value>, ...}
    state: OK | CERT | GAP
    entry: catalog/<category>/<name>.py     # OK and CERT rows; or ops/<category>/<name>.py
    contract_line: "<the cell (why + spec) or note sentence that decides coverage>"
    tier: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5                 # GAP rows: the sourcing rung
    candidate: torch.ops.trtllm.<name>      # GAP rows at tiers 1-3 (tier 3: flashinfer.<module>.<name>)
    tried: "<why tiers 1-3 do not serve it>"  # GAP rows at tiers 4-5
    call_sites:                             # where the target calls the entry
      - {site: "<Target.method, which step>", row_multiple: 1}
      - {site: "<...>", row_multiple: 6, gathered: true, row_width: 512}
      - {site: "<...>", eager_only: true}
queue:
  - {n: 1, mode: onboard, target: <category>/<name>, depends_on: []}
  - {n: 2, mode: verify,  target: <category>/<name>, depends_on: [],
      surface: "<the value the certified column excludes>",
      cells: [{<spec key>: <measured value>, ...}]}
  - {n: 3, mode: onboard, target: ops/<category>/<name>, depends_on: [],
      deployment: <name>}                # only a later deployment needs it
  - {n: 4, mode: verify,  target: <category>/<name>, depends_on: [],
      surface: "<...>", site: mtp_verify}  # optional: names its local copy
ceiling: null    # or {step: ..., searched: [...], why: ...}
```

Give every `call_sites` item the actual target method. `row_multiple` is how many rows one request brings there; `gathered: true` after attention-DP gathering, `eager_only: true` only outside captured paths.

Queue rules:

- `target` is `<category>/<name>` (a shared entry) or `ops/<category>/<name>` (the target's own), plain names; one row per entry: all its call sites' shapes go in its `cells`.
- `depends_on` lists the rows (`n`) whose entry this one calls.
- A `verify` row needs `surface`; it lists its `cells`, at most {{ max_cells }}: first those its deployment's options serve (its dtype, its limits), then the optional rest, one axis at a time (another dtype, the smallest and largest captured batch).
- `site` (lowercase words joined by `_`) names the local copy `<name>__<site>`; without it, `<name>__r<n>`. A target name never contains `__`.
- A row with no `deployment` key is `core`'s: the first deployment's options call its entry. A row only a later deployment's options call (another dtype, another member, disaggregation) names it and runs after `core`.
- Not for `not_done`: GPU tests, the boot, GSM8K (later tasks').

